id: com.charlieculbert.wclap-runtime-sine-example
name: WCLAP Runtime Sine Example
vendor: Charlie Culbert
version: 0.1.0
description: Minimal MIDI sine example
features:
  instrument
  synthesizer
  stereo
tests:
  test  checks
  descriptor-consistency  The factory and the created plug-in describe themselves the same way.
  features-categories  The plug-in declares what kind of plug-in it is.
  features-duplicates  No feature is declared twice.
  query-nonexistent-factory  Asking for a factory that does not exist returns nothing.
  create-id-with-trailing-garbage  An id the plug-in does not declare creates nothing.
  param-info-consistency  Parameter ids, ranges and flags agree with the specification.
  param-default-values  Every parameter starts at the default it declares.
  param-set-wrong-namespace  Events in an unknown namespace are ignored.
  param-modulation-value-unchanged  Modulation offsets the value heard without changing the value itself.
  param-modulation-polyphonic  Modulation addressed at one voice, one key, one channel, and all of them.
  param-modulation-reset  Modulation does not survive a reset.
  process-audio-basic  Five ordinary blocks produce usable audio.
  process-varying-block-sizes  Block sizes from one frame to four thousand.
  process-varying-sample-rates  Sample rates including fractional ones.
  process-random-block-sizes  Block sizes that change every block.
  state-invalid-empty  An empty state is not mistaken for a valid one.
  state-invalid-random  Random bytes do not crash the plug-in.
  state-round-trip  State saved and loaded returns the same parameters.
  state-buffered  State loads from a stream that returns short reads.
seed: 0x13376767
tests:
  test  status  seconds
  process-audio-basic  passed  @TIME@
